Produce a concise, cited assessment with a plain-language opening. It must add a useful bridge from the previously identified physical gap to the KS setting:

1. Distinguish momentum-dependent polarization, the cell-averaged first spin moment, anisotropic second moments and anisotropic stress. State what is actually required by the isotropic spin-fluid reduction; neither zero mean nor zero vorticity alone should be treated as the whole condition.
2. Work out, as far as supported, what homogeneous axisymmetric KS symmetry permits or excludes for these moments and stresses. Give a compact derivation or explicit mathematical check where feasible. Clearly mark assumed local/kinetic approximations; do not invent a microscopic closure or numerical relaxation coefficient.
