4. End with a narrow supported conclusion and the single smallest calculation or missing measurement that would resolve the remaining uncertainty. Do not claim that all effective-fluid bounces fail, that a nonzero momentum-space response proves net alignment, or that an unestablished assumption is a proven contradiction.

Target roughly 1,200–1,800 words plus a compact evidence table and any small calculation. The acceptance criterion is the quality and specificity of the transfer assessment, not reaching a positive/negative verdict or spending a token allowance. One worker only; reuse existing sources. No additional independent-review worker is automatically authorized for this extra branch. Tori may inspect and reconcile the result, but label its review status honestly.

