A radial mean spin is a special case: the Weyssenhoff shear–spin term vanishes because the two spherical shear eigenvalues are equal. Its spatial divergence also vanishes on a homogeneous KS slice. The report will distinguish this algebraic cancellation from physical validation; it does not determine the stress carried by microscopic spin correlations.
