+**B8 source custody and reproducibility · 2026-09-07.** This is the same single bounded native worker that wrote the report. No independent reviewer or additional worker was launched. All authored files and downloaded/rendered assets are inside `bounce/spin_polarization_20260907/`. B7 files and logs were neither opened nor edited. No shared finding, governing record, input dataset or external message was changed.
+
+The investigation read `../B5_VALIDITY_20260907.md`, `../KIMI_B5_CHALLENGE_20260907.md`, `../B6_APPLICABILITY_20260907.md`, `../b5_sources/access.json`, the specified publisher HTML, and the primary PDFs below. Prior reports are governing context, not substitutes for checking the primary equations. Kimi's references to Fu et al. and spin-relaxation papers were read as leads only; no physics claim here rests on those uninspected articles. The statement in Kimi's challenge that the bounce “lacks” a local-equilibrium expansion is not adopted as proof of failure: membership in that regime remains unestablished.
+
+| Primary article actually consulted | Copy and access | Equation/section checks |
+|---|---|---|
+| N. J. Popławski, *A nonsingular, anisotropic universe in a black hole with torsion and particle production*, GRG **53**, 18 (2021), DOI [10.1007/s10714-021-02790-7](https://doi.org/10.1007/s10714-021-02790-7) | Existing `../b4_springer_access.html`, publisher HTML; publication date displayed 7 February 2021. No arXiv substitution. | Extracted MathJax for Eqs. (1), (6), (10), (11), (15), (16), (24), (25), (28), (30), (34), (36), (37); read introduction and §§6–9, 11. The intrinsic sphere curvature is retained; source's approximate-scenario caveat retained. No new bounce classification. |
+| S. D. Brechet, M. P. Hobson, A. N. Lasenby, *Classical big-bounce cosmology: dynamical analysis of a homogeneous and irrotational Weyssenhoff fluid*, CQG **25**, 245016 (2008) | Existing `../b5_sources/brechet2008_publisher.pdf`; IOP publisher-formatted version held by [EPFL](https://infoscience.epfl.ch/server/api/core/bitstreams/66a4adbd-9c64-44ae-98ec-b323e021bc76/content). Repository delivery is distinguished from a manuscript. | §§2, 3.2, 4.3, Eqs. (8)–(13), (30)–(32), (52)–(53). Visually checked publisher pp. 4, 6, 9. Eq. (52) is conditional Weyssenhoff transport without the source's particle-production prescription. |
+| F. Becattini, M. Buzzegoli, A. Palermo, *Spin-thermal shear coupling in a relativistic fluid*, PLB **820**, 136519 (2021), DOI [10.1016/j.physletb.2021.136519](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physletb.2021.136519) | Existing `../b5_sources/becattini2021_publisher.pdf`; Elsevier publisher PDF through [SCOAP3](https://scoap3-prod-backend.s3.cern.ch/media/files/63428/10.1016/j.physletb.2021.136519_a.pdf). | §§2–4: long thermodynamic variation scales compared with operator correlation lengths; free/quasi-free restriction on Eq. (12); surface approximation Eq. (22); Eq. (23) and decomposition Eq. (24). Visually checked pp. 6–7. Non-dissipative LTE response; no relaxation coefficient is supplied. |
+| S. Y. F. Liu, Y. Yin, *Spin polarization induced by the hydrodynamic gradients*, JHEP **07** (2021) 188, DOI [10.1007/JHEP07(2021)188](https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP07(2021)188) | Existing `../b5_sources/liu_yin2021_publisher.pdf`; [Springer publisher PDF](https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/JHEP07%282021%29188.pdf). | §§2–3, 5.1–5.2: Eqs. (2.3), (2.7), (2.9), slow/fast limits (3.8), (3.11), coefficient (5.2), axial Wigner expression (5.4). Visually checked printed pp. 3–4 and 11 (PDF pages 4–5, 12). §3 notes its Wigner definition is not locally Lorentz covariant with metric perturbations; appropriate links enter a covariant definition, with the stated difference higher order in its derivative expansion. |
+| M. Buzzegoli, *Pseudogauge dependence of the spin polarization and of the axial vortical effect*, PRC **105**, 044907 (2022), DOI [10.1103/PhysRevC.105.044907](https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevC.105.044907) | **One new article acquired:** `buzzegoli2022_publisher.pdf`, APS version of record, published 22 April 2022. Fetched directly from [APS Harvest](https://harvest.aps.org/v2/journals/articles/10.1103/PhysRevC.105.044907/fulltext), HTTP 200, 315839 bytes. | Introduction, §§IV.A–B and VI; Eqs. (39)–(43). Visually checked pp. 044907-9 and -10. Eq. (43) cancels the BBP shear term for the specified GLW/HW LTE constructions. No claim that a change of notation changes observables in one fixed fully specified state. |
+
